              = succeed "," do
                %em On Arithmetic Modular Categories
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.2229"} arXiv:1305.2229
          %h3#relation_to_3dcs2dwzw_quantum_field_theory Relation to 3dCS/2dWZW quantum field theory
          %p
            Discussion of modular tensor categories in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} CS/WZW correspondence
          %p A general survey of the literature is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Rowell"}> Eric Rowell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From quantum groups to Unitary modular tensor categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503226"} arXiv:math/0503226
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"}> Victor Ostrik
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor categories in conformal field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://pages.uoregon.edu/vostrik/talks/beijing.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p
            More specific discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FuchsRunkelSchweigert02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Runkel"} Ingo Runkel
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
                %em TFT construction of RCFT correlators I: partition functions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204148"}> arXiv:hep-th/0204148
                )
              %p
                (for more along these lines see at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRS+formalism"} FRS formalism
          %p
            Review of construction of MTCs from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebras"} vertex operator algebras
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Lepowsky"}> James Lepowsky
              ,
              %em From the representation theory of vertex operator algebras to modular tensor categories in conformal field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.pnas.org/content/102/15/5304.full.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            (see also the discussion at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"}> Bruce Bartlett
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Douglas"} Christopher Douglas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"} Chris Schommer-Pries
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
              %em Modular categories as representations of the 3-dimensional bordism 2-category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1509.06811"}> arXiv:1509.06811
              )
          %p
            On the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Drinfeld+center"} Drinfeld center
          %ul
            %li#GuuTham21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jin-Cheng+Guu"}> Jin-Cheng Guu
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ying+Hong+Tham"} Ying Hong Tham
              %em Explicit Factorization of a Categorical Center
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.06919"}> arXiv:2111.06919
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#AnyonicTopologicalOrderInTermsOfBraidedFusionCategoriesReferences Anyonic topological order in terms of braided fusion categories
            %h4#claim_and_status Claim and status
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+theory"} condensed matter theory
              it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
              that species of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyon"} anyonic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
              correspond to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+categories"} braided
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+fusion+category"} unitary
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+categories"} fusion categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+categories"} modular tensor categories
            %p The origin of the claim is:
            %ul
              %li#Kitaev06
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kitaev"}> Alexei Kitaev
                , Section 8 and Appendix E of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anyons in an exactly solved model and beyond
                %strong 321
                1 (2006) 2-111 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aop.2005.10.005"}> doi:10.1016/j.aop.2005.10.005
                ]
            %p Early accounts re-stating this claim (without attribution):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chetan+Nayak"}> Chetan Nayak
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+H.+Simon"} Steven H. Simon
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ady+Stern"} Ady Stern
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Freedman"} Michael Freedman
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sankar+Das+Sarma"} Sankar Das Sarma
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Non-Abelian Anyons and Topological Quantum Computation
                  %strong 80
                  1083 (2008) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.80.1083"}> doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.80.1083
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.1889"} arXiv:0707.1888
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhenghan+Wang"}> Zhenghan Wang
                  , Section 6.3 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topological Quantum Computation
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 112
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/publications/authors/books/postpub/cbms-112"} ISBN-13: 978-0-8218-4930-9]
            %p Further discussion (mostly review and mostly without attribution):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Burton"}> Simon Burton
                  ,
                  %em A Short Guide to Anyons and Modular Functors
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.05384"}> arXiv:1610.05384
                  ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (this one stands out as still attributing the claim to
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "#Kitaev06"} Kitaev (2006), Appendix E
              %li#RowellWang18
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+C.+Rowell"}> Eric C. Rowell
                  ,
